\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want to be an  artist}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Artist is a condition to be cured.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Syptom of a deep and totalizing selfishness.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 A symptom of having no one who understands you. No one who agrees with you.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want to be an artist}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Why not?}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t look at me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram smiled. }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\ul\ulc0 The fat swerve of his bottom lip looked like a worm-baited hook had snagged his tawny beard. }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He said, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So exaggerated is the artist\u8217\'92s sense of self that it becomes impossible to describe them without resorting to sarcasm.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re still looking at me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There is no one else here.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Two slaves stood at attention by the kitchen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s double-swing doors. Vigram\u8217\'92s blindness to their existence was cruel, but this did not dismantle his point, }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I feel like we\u8217\'92re talking past each other,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Because anyone can be anything. I mean\u8230\'85and this is hard to articulate\u8230\'85well, maybe not. What I mean is, you can\u8217\'92t ever really know what\u8217\'92s going on inside someone else\u8217\'92s head, not enough to really know who they are. You identify who they are based on their works; the things they make. A farmer farms. A tax collector collects taxes. An artist arts.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93An artist }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 arts}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93An artist makes art.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But what }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 is}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  art? This is my point\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 you cannot say. It is impossible to build a wall with words around the physical objects of human creation which . You cannot say what separates an \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91art object\u8217\'92 from an ordinary object.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I think you can.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Go on, then.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, it\u8217\'92s hard to articulate. But I think it has something to do with selfishness.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Does it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 as Mandri did think highly of himself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Why shouldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t he?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 When he was ten, he could paint a portrait in oils that rivaled the old Jeketian masters. These weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t polish-jobs where the paint was thin and every hair was rendered into being like he\u8217\'92d lost the plot of reality. By his hand, a single stroke of umber was enough to define the chestnut skin, the high-arched cheek, the skull underneath, the light, the shadow, even the mood of the piece. Warms and cools in one single stroke! With twenty-four, he could find a vivid likeness. There might be a few extra nibbles to make a beauty\u8217\'92s eyes glisten and her cleavage heave, but nobody counted those. Well, Vigram counted them. Lascivious men counted them. Probably, every man counted them. Some women, presumably.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 And like any prideful artist, Mandri would strut around the grand Hrkan galleries and make clear his contempt for his contemporaries. He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d stand in front of a painting and say, \u8220\'93This piece really moves me,\u8221\'94 and he\u8217\'92d make a show of walking away. All must bear witness to his mop of black hair as it flounced itself in time with his skinny, stiff-backed step. Or he\u8217\'92d say, \u8220\'93I weep at every stroke,\u8221\'94 and he\u8217\'92d flash a knowing smile. Back in those days, he\u8217\'92d say these things directly to a fellow artist\u8217\'92s face if he could get to it. He never thought of it as bullying because artists, like himself, were safe targets for playful derision; it wasn\u8217\'92t the person he was making fun of, it was their failed attempts to express themselves, and those were completely different things. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never go after the person.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 No, never.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Artists were the best people. They needed tough skin, unearned confidence, and a flair for the dramatic. Without any of that, an artist stays obscure. Then there\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s the servility. Above all, an artist must be servile to the hand that feeds. And look at that, Vigram had a lot of food at his table.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said confidently, \u8220\'93you are an idiot.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0}